[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b21: morphology vs footprint
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   step_b20 found the detached cluster is a plateau, not a
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   peak: flat inside the 60 deg cap, depleted ring at 60-90,
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   uniform far field -- top-hat beats von Mises on AIC.
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   But is the morphology itself footprint-explicable?  The
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   ring region (varpi ~ 109-139 and ~319-349 deg) sits far
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   from the detached discovery-footprint centre (~10 deg), so
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   pointing could plausibly produce BOTH the flat interior
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   (smeared pile-up near the footprint) AND the ring deficit
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   (objects rarely discovered with perihelia there).
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   The test: generate conditional-null realizations of the
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   detached varpi sample -- each object draws (Om,w) from
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   controls discovered within +-30 deg of ITS OWN opposition
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   longitude (the b8 machinery, which inherits the measured
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   footprint and footprint->elements map at full strength) --
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   and ask what morphology the null produces.
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   K1  Expected |varpi - axis| profile under the conditional
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   null vs observed.
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   K2  Null distribution of (AIC_tophat - AIC_vm): does the
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   footprint also prefer the top-hat?  If the null prefers
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   von Mises/uniform while the data prefer the top-hat,
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   the morphology is an independent datum; if the null
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   produces top-hats too, it is not.
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   K3  How often does the null produce a 60-90 deg ring as
[2026-09-21 14:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 056]   depleted as observed (<= 4 objects)?
